Chapter: ScenerySpec
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Safari chapter Scenery
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 Scenery: the vocabulary three populations share.

 Two constants, two records, two enumerations and one predicate. The predicate is
 the only code, and it is a six-way dispatch where five arms answer the same
 thing -- which is exactly the shape that hides a mis-wired arm, because getting
 five of six right by accident is easy and the sixth is the only one anybody
 sees. So all six are graded, not just the True one.

 EVERY CONSTRUCTOR IS FORCED THROUGH THE FRONT END HERE, which is most of what
 this file is for. Scheme and Creature are pure enumerations with no arithmetic
 anywhere near them: nothing about them can be wrong except that an arm fails to
 accept the declaration or the `when` that reads it. A chapter of type
 declarations is only compiled when something uses it.

 THE COLLISION THE CHAPTER RECORDS IS WORTH A LINE. The constructor is `DuckPond`
 and not `Pond` because chapters share one flat namespace inside a bundle
 (CDX3001) and `Safari chapter Pond` is already in this port -- a collision that
 appears only once something cites both. This spec cites Scenery and the sibling
 PondSpec cites Pond, so the two are compiled separately and neither would find
 it; what finds it is the game bundle, which cites both, and this note is here so
 the next person does not "simplify" the name.

 We say:

Section: The Road

  road-got : List Real
  road-got = [lane-width, herd-road-offset]

  road-want : List Real
  road-want = [4.0, 10.0]

Section: The Predicate, All Six Arms

 DuckPond is the only True. The other five are graded because a dispatch that
 answers True for Rhino would be invisible to any test that only asked about
 ponds.

  pond-got : List Boolean
  pond-got = [is-pond DuckPond, is-pond NoCreature, is-pond Elephant, is-pond Giraffe, is-pond Zebra, is-pond Rhino]

  pond-want : List Boolean
  pond-want = [True, False, False, False, False, False]

Section: The Enumerations

 Scheme has no reader in this chapter, so one is written here. That is the point:
 without it the three constructors are declared and never used, and a declaration
 nothing reads is a declaration nothing compiles.

  scheme-code : Scheme -> Integer
  scheme-code (s) =
   when s
    is AllGreen -> 0
    is YellowGreen -> 1
    is RedGreen -> 2

  creature-code : Creature -> Integer
  creature-code (c) =
   when c
    is NoCreature -> 0
    is Elephant -> 1
    is Giraffe -> 2
    is Zebra -> 3
    is Rhino -> 4
    is DuckPond -> 5

  code-got : List Integer
  code-got = [scheme-code AllGreen, scheme-code YellowGreen, scheme-code RedGreen, creature-code NoCreature, creature-code Elephant, creature-code Giraffe, creature-code Zebra, creature-code Rhino, creature-code DuckPond]

  code-want : List Integer
  code-want = [0, 1, 2, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

Section: The Records

 A Tree and a Critter with distinct field values, so a field read from its
 neighbour shows. The Critter is the one carrying a Boolean and an Integer
 codepoint beside its Reals, which is the mixed-type record in this chapter.

  a-tree : Tree
  a-tree = Tree { along = 120.5, across = 3.25, color = 9066271, height = 7.75 }

  a-critter : Critter
  a-critter = Critter { along = 250.5, across = -6.5, codepoint = 128004, height = 1.375, face-right = True }

  rec-reals-got : List Real
  rec-reals-got = [a-tree.along, a-tree.across, a-tree.height, a-critter.along, a-critter.across, a-critter.height]

  rec-reals-want : List Real
  rec-reals-want = [120.5, 3.25, 7.75, 250.5, -6.5, 1.375]

  rec-ints-got : List Integer
  rec-ints-got = [a-tree.color, a-critter.codepoint]

  rec-ints-want : List Integer
  rec-ints-want = [9066271, 128004]

  rec-bools-got : List Boolean
  rec-bools-got = [a-critter.face-right]

  rec-bools-want : List Boolean
  rec-bools-want = [True]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "sc-road" road-got road-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "sc-pond" pond-got pond-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "sc-code" code-got code-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "sc-recr" rec-reals-got rec-reals-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "sc-reci" rec-ints-got rec-ints-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "sc-recb" rec-bools-got rec-bools-want)
  end
